Description: Modern Linux screen-time enforcement daemon (Timekpr-nExT fork)
 curfewd is a drop-in maintained fork of Timekpr-nExT that tracks and limits
 computer usage for user accounts on Linux desktops.
 .
 It fixes broken screen-lock enforcement on Linux Mint Cinnamon, XFCE, and
 MATE, handles fullscreen X11 games holding input grabs, preserves full
 compatibility with existing /etc/timekpr and /var/lib/timekpr configs,
 and provides both curfewctl and timekpra CLI tools.
 .
 Report bugs at: https://github.com/csmende/curfewd/issues
